# Reachability opt-out — CONSUMER POLICY (scripts/gate-reachability.sh).
#
# The sweep FAILS any check no root invokes: a gate that runs on nobody's
# schedule runs after the incident. This file is the only way to say "yes,
# and deliberately so" — one entry per line, `<path> -- <one-line reason>`.
#
# THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY, and empty is a statement, not an
# omission: every check in this repository is reached by a root today.
# The five that were not on 2026-08-02 — the fact-health, session-digest,
# instruments and whisper gates, and the battery's own mutation gate —
# were WIRED rather than excused (scripts/release-battery.sh arms 7-9),
# because each had a schedule available to it and only lacked the line.
# An ABSENT file would leave the sweep unable to tell a deliberate
# exemption from an oversight and make it say so on every run; an empty
# one arms the policy and states the position out loud.
#
# Fail modes are copied from .truth/generated-paths on purpose:
#   ABSENT    — no policy; nothing is excused and an advisory is voiced.
#   EMPTY     — armed and silent: everything here must be reachable.
#   POPULATED — armed: the listed paths are reported, not failed.
#
# Two guards against the excuse outliving its reason, both enforced by the
# sweep: an entry naming a path that is not a check FAILS, and an entry
# naming a check that has SINCE become reachable FAILS. A standing excuse
# nobody rechecks is the dark gate wearing a permission slip.
#
# Lines starting ':', '-' or '!' are refused (SI-1, as in
# .truth/citation-scope): exemptions are enumerated positively, never as
# exclusions, so nobody can waive a whole tree with one character.
#
# Add a line here the day a check genuinely has no root — and say why.

# --- SECOND KEY SPACE: not-a-check --------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-28 with the complement assertion in the sweep. The first key
# space answers "this CHECK is unreachable, and deliberately so". This one
# answers the opposite question, which the sweep could not ask until now:
# "a root reaches this file and the CHECK patterns do not name it -- is that
# an unmeasured gate, or not a gate at all?"
#
# The question had never been asked, and the answer was three live gates
# outside the measure: scripts/check-truth.sh (THE COMMIT GATE),
# scripts/retracted-figures.sh, and scripts/truth-whisper.py. All three are
# now in the CHECK patterns. What remains below is the honest residue.
#
# MIRROR RULE, as everywhere here: an entry naming a path the CHECK patterns
# DO name, or a path no root reaches, is itself a FAILURE. A declaration that
# outlived its finding is a gate that looks considered and covers nothing.

not-a-check:scripts/truth -- the CLI itself, reached because hooks invoke it to file and fold records. It is the thing gates are ABOUT, not a gate: it refuses at intake, but those refusals are the subject of the canary's seeded faults, not of reachability
not-a-check:template/scripts/truth -- the template-side mirror of the same CLI, reached through install-hooks.sh writing consumer hook bodies. Same reason
not-a-check:scripts/truth-session-digest.py -- the SessionStart hook body. It REPORTS a digest to an agent starting work; it asserts nothing and can fail nothing, which is the census definition of a reporter (docs/governance/catch-log.md)
not-a-check:template/scripts/truth-bd-adapter.sh -- the ADR-004 tracker adapter seam. It translates between the ledger and an external tracker; a translation layer has no verdict to give
